@startuml tailscale-nat-hole-punching
participant "Phone\n(behind carrier NAT)" as Phone
participant "STUN server" as Stun
participant "Home router\n(NAT)" as Router
participant "Cluster node" as Cluster

Phone -> Stun : query public IP:port
Stun --> Phone : 203.0.113.5:54321

Cluster -> Stun : query public IP:port
Stun --> Cluster : 177.x.x.x:41641

par simultaneous send
  Phone -> Router : UDP to 177.x.x.x:41641
  Router -> Cluster : forwarded / NAT state created
else
  Cluster -> Phone : UDP to 203.0.113.5:54321
end

note over Phone, Cluster
  Each NAT device creates a state entry
  for its own outbound packet, which then
  accepts the matching inbound reply.
  Direct WireGuard tunnel now open.
end note

note over Phone
  Symmetric NAT (common on carrier
  networks) assigns a different external
  port per destination -> the port the
  cluster expects never matches -> hole
  punch fails -> falls back to DERP.
end note
@enduml
